From 2a6faf63a792c477c5cb7218a4807751238b73bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:02:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban chat links: links_diff leaves out machine
 chats; a released sibling no longer settles a closed card

laptop-1 runs kanban.sync.links_reader=replica while links_diff('macbook')
was not clean: 270 only-in-ledger links across 140 chats (02:54 PST
2026-11-13, core fedc433cef). The module says readers switch only once the
diff is clean, so a real divergence (the courier-link gap, t_01a1d47a4f8f5545)
blended into the noise. Read-only classification over tailnet (card
t_01a1d488bea784e9):

1. 250 links / 137 chats: kanban worker transcripts (machine sessions).
   _ledger_links never writes a machine session's link and reconcile releases
   one, so the ledger's rows for them (242 legacy aliases, 8 qualified) were
   differences by construction. links_diff now leaves the chats the writer
   never links (_unlinked_chats: machine sessions, placeholders; the same
   machine_sessions call _ledger_links makes) out of both sides and reports
   them as machine_links.

2. 19 links / 1 chat (20261026_170127_f07c32): done hub cards whose ledger
   obligation is unverified (origin_obligations.released=0), so the chat's
   gateway keeps the `created` link unreleased. Their owner-written
   `shepherd` sibling was released when the card closed, and replica_cards'
   chat_released rule (9d13eeb47e) then dropped the card. That rule assumed
   the released sibling carried a verified release. Its own incident (an
   owner-written `created` link nobody released, 2026-11-01) has been fixed
   on the writer side since 3cc6ce09c8 (_owner_written_releases), so the rule
   only fired where the ledger still held the link open. Removed: each link
   carries its own answer, as replica_cards documents ("only a released link
   drops it"), and the replica keeps a done-but-unverified card `unknown`
   like the ledger.

3. 1 link: hub card t_d3e3f88a on the bb-tuner profile's own board, which
   the Board does not carry (link rejected not_found). A real replica gap,
   still counted; follow-up t_01a1d49646d816af.

What-if on laptop-1 with both changes applied read-only: only_in_ledger 1
(cause 3), only_in_replica 1 (a card created minutes before, ledger lag).

Tests: test_kanban_chat_links_parity.py adds
test_links_diff_agrees_on_a_done_unverified_card_whose_owner_written_sibling_was_released
and test_links_diff_leaves_out_chats_the_link_writer_never_links (both fail
on main); test_kanban_chat_links.py's sibling test now asserts the
unreleased link stays an `unknown` obligation.
